rary/bg/7/\",\"title\":\"Chapter Seven: Knowledge of the Absolute\"}],\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/13/\",\"bb\":1937,\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"pager\":{\"previous\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/12/\",\"title\":\"TEXT 12\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]},\"next\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/14/\",\"title\":\"TEXT 14\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]}},\"child_items\":[{\"section\":\"devanagari\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.devanagari\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.DevanagariRecord\",\"title\":\"devanagari\",\"id\":2187,\"bb\":568162,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/13/devanagari/\",\"body_final\":\"त्रिभिर्गुणमयैर्भावैरेभि: सर्वमिदं जगत् ।
मोहितं नाभिजानाति मामेभ्य: परमव्ययम् ॥ १३ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2188,\"bb\":1938,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/13/b1938/\",\"body_value\":\"tribhir guṇa-mayair bhāvair
ebhiḥ sarvam idaṁ jagat
mohitaṁ nābhijānāti
mām ebhyaḥ param avyayam\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":2189,\"bb\":1939,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/13/b1939/\",\"shadow_value\":\"tribhiḥ – three; guṇa-mayaiḥ – consisting of the guṇas; bhāvaiḥ – by the states of being; ebhiḥ – all these; sarvam – whole; idam – this; jagat – universe; mohitam – deluded; na abhijānāti – does not know; mām – Me; ebhyaḥ – above these; param – the Supreme; avyayam – inexhaustible.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"tribhiḥ\",\"translation\":\"three\"},{\"word\":\"guṇa-mayaiḥ\",\"translation\":\"consisting of the guṇas\"},{\"word\":\"bhāvaiḥ\",\"translation\":\"by the states of being\"},{\"word\":\"ebhiḥ\",\"translation\":\"all these\"},{\"word\":\"sarvam\",\"translation\":\"whole\"},{\"word\":\"idam\",\"translation\":\"this\"},{\"word\":\"jagat\",\"translation\":\"universe\"},{\"word\":\"mohitam\",\"translation\":\"deluded\"},{\"word\":\"na abhijānāti\",\"translation\":\"does not know\"},{\"word\":\"mām\",\"translation\":\"Me\"},{\"word\":\"ebhyaḥ\",\"translation\":\"above these\"},{\"word\":\"param\",\"translation\":\"the Supreme\"},{\"word\":\"avyayam\",\"translation\":\"inexhaustible\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":2190,\"bb\":1940,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/13/b1940/\",\"body_value\":\"Deluded by the three modes [goodness, passion and ignorance], the whole world does not know Me, who am above the modes and inexhaustible.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2191,\"bb\":1941,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/13/b1941/\",\"body_value\":\"The whole world is enchanted by the three modes of material nature. Those who are bewildered by these three modes cannot understand that transcendental to this material nature is the Supreme Lord, Kṛṣṇa.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2192,\"bb\":1942,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/13/b1942/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2193,\"bb\":1943,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/7/13/b1943/\",\"body_value\":\"There are many different kinds of living entities – human beings, demigods, animals, etc. – and each and every one of them is under the influence of material nature, and all of them have forgotten the transcendent Personality of Godhead. Those who are in the modes of passion and ignorance, and even those who are in the mode of goodness, cannot go beyond the impersonal Brahman conception of the Absolute Truth. They are bewildered before the Supreme Lord in His personal feature, which possesses all beauty, opulence, knowledge, strength, fame and renunciation. When even those who are in goodness cannot understand, what hope is there for those in passion and ignorance? Kṛṣṇa consciousness is transcendental to all these three modes of material nature, and those who are truly established in Kṛṣṇa consciousness are actually liberated.\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 7.13\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 7.13\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n30:I[78455,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0